# MF Overhaul 0.4.0: user: "make everything realistic in colour palette and physics, no shortcuts". Rules applied to every
#   particle family the overhaul had not yet touched (burst smoke / dust / earth were done in 57-59_realism):
#   SOLIDS fall under real gravity (c6 y -9.8), light things with drag (leaves -2, hay -1.5); earth takes the soil palette
#   (black earth 0x4C4D41 / clay 0x4E4332 / mud 0x8D7D63 from season soils c6), debris takes plaster-grey.
#   DUST drifts with the wind, settles slowly (-0.02 .. -0.03), spins little (40 deg), takes the lightened field/mud tone 0xA89C7E.
#   HOT SMOKE is buoyant (+0.05 .. +0.3, the hotter the faster) and sooty: burning fuel / vehicles near-black brown, HE on steel
#   dark grey; coloured signal smoke keeps its hue; spin 360 -> 60 everywhere (a full turn reads as rotating puffs).
#   WATER: spray under gravity (-9.8), columns -5; colours unchanged. Flashes untouched.
